# Firebase Functions params (firebase-functions/params defineString).
# Non-secret config - safe to commit. Read at deploy time so
# `firebase deploy --non-interactive` has explicit values instead of
# prompting for the code defaults.
#
# WebAuthn (ADR-0014):
#   The RPID is derived per-request from the caller's Origin and each
#   ceremony verifies against every allow-listed origin's host, so one
#   deploy serves both localhost and the hosted origin. A passkey is bound
#   to the host it was registered on, so testers re-register per environment
#   (inherent to WebAuthn).
#
#   * WEBAUTHN_PRODUCTION_ORIGIN - canonical hosted origin; listing it here
#     allow-lists it and makes its host a valid RPID. ('...firebaseapp.com'
#     is a different host - add it to STAGING_ORIGINS if used, or redirect.)
#   * WEBAUTHN_STAGING_ORIGINS - extra allow-listed origins (the localhost
#     ports Flutter web binds; use --web-port=5173 for a stable dev origin).
#   * WEBAUTHN_RPID - static fallback RPID for callers whose Origin isn't on
#     the allow-list (e.g. non-browser); browser ceremonies ignore it.
#
# Mobile (Android/iOS) is not affected by these values: the app's
# WebauthnAvailableProvider short-circuits to false off-web, so mobile
# uses biometric + PIN exclusively. WebAuthn is a web-only fallback.
WEBAUTHN_PRODUCTION_ORIGIN=https://csc234-user-centric-mobile-app.web.app
WEBAUTHN_STAGING_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:4200,http://localhost:4000,http://localhost:5000,http://localhost:7357,http://localhost:8000,http://localhost:8080,http://localhost:8888,http://localhost:9000,http://localhost:9090,http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://127.0.0.1:4200,http://127.0.0.1:5000,http://127.0.0.1:8000,http://127.0.0.1:8080
WEBAUTHN_RPID=localhost
